{
  "task": "Write Python 3 function solve(rows). First apply an audit filter to the ORIGINAL input positions, indexed from zero: omit positions whose index modulo 5 equals 3, except always retain the last input position. Rotate the retained rows LEFT by 2 positions modulo the retained length (empty stays empty). Apply the following rules to that transformed list: Rows are [capacity,request] with nonnegative integers. Process sequentially, with a starting shared budget of 17. Each allocation is min(capacity,request,remaining budget). Return allocations; never replenish budget.\nReturn the requested value, without printing. Inputs follow the types specified. Do not mutate the input. Standard library is allowed.",
  "specification": "First apply an audit filter to the ORIGINAL input positions, indexed from zero: omit positions whose index modulo 5 equals 3, except always retain the last input position. Rotate the retained rows LEFT by 2 positions modulo the retained length (empty stays empty). Apply the following rules to that transformed list: Rows are [capacity,request] with nonnegative integers. Process sequentially, with a starting shared budget of 17. Each allocation is min(capacity,request,remaining budget). Return allocations; never replenish budget.",
  "reference": "def solve(rows):\n left=17; out=[]\n for cap,req in rows:\n  v=min(cap,req,left);out.append(v);left-=v\n return out\n_core_solve=solve\ndef solve(rows):\n filtered=[row for i,row in enumerate(rows) if i%5!=3 or i==len(rows)-1]\n if filtered:\n  shift=2%len(filtered)\n  filtered=filtered[shift:]+filtered[:shift]\n return _core_solve(filtered)",
  "mutation": "def solve(rows):\n left=17; out=[]\n for cap,req in rows:\n  v=min(cap,req,max(1,left));out.append(v);left-=v\n return out\n_core_solve=solve\ndef solve(rows):\n filtered=[row for i,row in enumerate(rows) if i%5!=3 or i==len(rows)-1]\n if filtered:\n  shift=2%len(filtered)\n  filtered=filtered[shift:]+filtered[:shift]\n return _core_solve(filtered)",
